<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/bootstrap/processes/ns#"
                  xmlns:cat-harness.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/processes/ns#"
                  id="Definitions_BeanLifecycle"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows">

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Agent bean lifecycle — folio-assistant
       Issue: https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/203

       BEANS ARE FOR AGENTS. They hold process state for work an agent
       is doing, in a store that is committed so a sibling session sees
       it. A human's own reminders are TODOS and are a different thing
       with a different cycle; see the todos-vs-beans page.

       A BEAN IS NEVER DELETED. `beans delete` exists in the CLI, which
       is exactly why the prohibition has to be written where an agent
       reads rather than left implied. Work that turns out not to be
       wanted is SCRAPPED, with its reasons — the record of having
       considered and rejected something is worth as much as the record
       of having done it, and a sibling session that finds an id gone
       cannot tell abandonment from accident.

       TWO LAYERS, and confusing them is how a step comes to announce an
       effect it does not have. `claim`, `note` and `resolve` are what
       the WORKFLOW ENGINE performs on a process instance's own bean
       when a step completes. Creating, scrapping and editing are the
       AGENT's own `beans` CLI calls; the engine has no op for them.
       An earlier diagram carried `<cat-harness.processes:bean action="create"/>`, which
       the engine never read — `op` is the attribute — so the step
       silently did nothing for weeks.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <bpmn:process id="Process_BeanLifecycle" name="Agent bean lifecycle" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>The whole life of a work-plan item, and the rules that make one agent's bean legible to another: check before you create, claim before you work, keep the body current as you go, and end it in a state that says why.

You are in this process the moment durable work is identified — which is before the first tool call, not after the work is done. The second lane exists because a bean you did not open is not yours to close: coordination replaces a decision you are not entitled to make.

The one irreversible thing is refused outright. Unwanted work is SCRAPPED with its reasons, never deleted, because a scrapped bean stops the next agent re-entering a dead end while a deleted one leaves a sibling unable to tell abandonment from accident.</bpmn:documentation>

    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_BeanLifecycle">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Agent" name="Agent (this session)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Owns every transition on a bean it holds — check, create, claim, work, and the three-way outcome at the end — but GW_Owner is the one branch this lane cannot complete itself: the moment a bean turns out to be someone else's, the only correct move is to leave the whole lifecycle to Lane_Sibling rather than resolve, scrap or edit it from here.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="authoring-agent"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_DurableWork</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_CheckExists</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Exists</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Create</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Owner</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Claim</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Work</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>GW_Outcome</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Complete</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Scrap</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RecordBlocker</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_Recorded</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Sibling" name="Sibling session or human (not yours to close)">
        <bpmn:documentation>The only task in this diagram with no `cat-harness.processes:bean` op at all — every other terminal action here writes something, and this one's entire job is to write nothing to a bean it does not own, ending the lifecycle at End_NotYours rather than at the completion Lane_Agent reaches for its own beans.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:role ref="sibling-session"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_LeaveAlone</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_NotYours</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_DurableWork" name="Durable work&#10;identified"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_CheckExists" name="Check before you create&#10;(exact-title search)">
      <bpmn:documentation>STRICT. `beans create` is not idempotent: it mints a
fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing, so re-entering a step duplicates
the plan instead of no-op'ing. In the qou folio an unguarded re-run produced
14,688 duplicate beans — 92% of every open bean — which starved the
idle-backlog policy of signal and collided with 15 real ids.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Exists" name="Already exists?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered by the exact-title check before it (`todo-manager` §'Check before you create'): `beans list --json --search` followed by an exact comparison of titles, since `--search` is fuzzy. `no` (0 exact matches) creates the bean. `yes` (1 or more) does not create a second one — `beans create` mints a fresh id every call and dedupes on nothing — and asks whose the existing bean is.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Create" name="Create the bean&#10;(agent CLI, not an engine op)">
      <bpmn:documentation>`beans create &quot;&lt;title&gt;&quot;`. This is the AGENT's call.
The workflow engine has no `create` op — its vocabulary is claim, note and
resolve, all of which act on an instance's existing bean.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Owner" name="Whose bean?">
      <bpmn:documentation>Answered from the existing bean and its surroundings (`bean-coordination`). `someone else's` means a sibling is mid-flight on it: a claim naming a branch, a recent note, or an open PR. That bean is left alone and the lifecycle ends here. `mine / unclaimed` claims it. A claim is branch-local, so check the bean's status on origin/main and the open PRs naming it, not only the copy on your branch.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_LeaveAlone" name="Leave it alone&#10;(coordinate instead)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Never resolve, scrap or delete a bean another session
or a human owns. Claiming is how two sessions avoid picking the same item;
closing someone else's is how one of them loses work it had not finished
reporting.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_NotYours" name="Not yours to close"/>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Claim" name="Claim it&#10;(status: in-progress)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Idempotent. Claim BEFORE working, and note the branch,
so a sibling session can see the item is taken rather than discovering it by
collision.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="claim"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Work" name="Work, keeping the body current&#10;(this is 'edit')">
      <bpmn:documentation>Editing a bean is not a separate ceremony: check off
todo items as they happen, append measurements with the command and date that
produced them, and record what you now know that the next agent does not. A
bean whose body is a title is a placeholder, not a plan.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_Outcome" name="Outcome?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The performer's judgement on the work, and one of three recorded endings. `done`: complete it only when no todo is unchecked, with a summary of what changed. `not wanted`: set it `scrapped` with a 'Reasons for Scrapping' section — never delete. `blocked`: record what it waits on with `--blocked-by`, say what would unblock it, and return it to `todo`, because an in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work.</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Complete" name="Complete&#10;(no unchecked todos left)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Only once nothing is unchecked, and with a summary of
what changed. The engine's `resolve` completes a bean only after the instance
itself has completed — whether work is done is a judgement, and a bean is not
closed on someone else's say-so.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="resolve"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_Scrap" name="Scrap with reasons&#10;NEVER delete">
      <bpmn:documentation>`status: scrapped`, plus a "Reasons for Scrapping"
section. This is what "disable" means here — the CLI has no disabled state;
its vocabulary is draft, todo, in-progress, completed, scrapped.

DELETION IS NEVER THE ANSWER, even though `beans delete` exists. A scrapped
bean records that the work was considered and rejected, and why; a deleted one
leaves a sibling session unable to tell abandonment from accident, and leaves
the next agent free to re-open the same dead end.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="todo-manager"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:task id="Task_RecordBlocker" name="Record the blocker&#10;and hand back">
      <bpmn:documentation>Blocked is not scrapped. Set `--blocked-by`, say in the
body what would unblock it, and return it to `todo` so it is visible to whoever
can act. An in-progress bean nobody is progressing reads as active work.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <bootstrap.processes:skill ref="bean-coordination"/>
        <cat-harness.processes:bean op="note"/>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
    </bpmn:task>

    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_Recorded" name="State recorded"/>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_1" sourceRef="Start_DurableWork" targetRef="Task_CheckExists"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_2" sourceRef="Task_CheckExists" targetRef="GW_Exists"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_3" name="no" sourceRef="GW_Exists" targetRef="Task_Create"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_4" name="yes" sourceRef="GW_Exists" targetRef="GW_Owner"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_5" name="someone else's" sourceRef="GW_Owner" targetRef="Task_LeaveAlone"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_6" sourceRef="Task_LeaveAlone" targetRef="End_NotYours"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_7" name="mine / unclaimed" sourceRef="GW_Owner" targetRef="Task_Claim"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_8" sourceRef="Task_Create" targetRef="Task_Claim"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_9" sourceRef="Task_Claim" targetRef="Task_Work"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_10" sourceRef="Task_Work" targetRef="GW_Outcome"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_11" name="done" sourceRef="GW_Outcome" targetRef="Task_Complete"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_12" name="not wanted" sourceRef="GW_Outcome" targetRef="Task_Scrap"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_13" name="blocked" sourceRef="GW_Outcome" targetRef="Task_RecordBlocker"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_14" sourceRef="Task_Complete" targetRef="End_Recorded"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_15" sourceRef="Task_Scrap" targetRef="End_Recorded"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="BF_16" sourceRef="Task_RecordBlocker" targetRef="End_Recorded"/>
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_BeanLifecycle">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_BeanLifecycle" bpmnElement="Process_BeanLifecycle">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Agent_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Agent" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1560" height="300"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Sibling_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Sibling" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="380" width="1560" height="160"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_DurableWork_di" bpmnElement="Start_DurableWork"><dc:Bounds x="220" y="190" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_CheckExists_di" bpmnElement="Task_CheckExists"><dc:Bounds x="300" y="168" width="150" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Exists_di" bpmnElement="GW_Exists"><dc:Bounds x="490" y="183" width="50" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Create_di" bpmnElement="Task_Create"><dc:Bounds x="580" y="108" width="150" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Owner_di" bpmnElement="GW_Owner"><dc:Bounds x="620" y="253" width="50" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Claim_di" bpmnElement="Task_Claim"><dc:Bounds x="780" y="168" width="150" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Work_di" bpmnElement="Task_Work"><dc:Bounds x="970" y="168" width="160" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="GW_Outcome_di" bpmnElement="GW_Outcome"><dc:Bounds x="1170" y="183" width="50" height="50"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Complete_di" bpmnElement="Task_Complete"><dc:Bounds x="1270" y="98" width="160" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Scrap_di" bpmnElement="Task_Scrap"><dc:Bounds x="1270" y="188" width="160" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RecordBlocker_di" bpmnElement="Task_RecordBlocker"><dc:Bounds x="1270" y="278" width="160" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_Recorded_di" bpmnElement="End_Recorded"><dc:Bounds x="1500" y="190" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_LeaveAlone_di" bpmnElement="Task_LeaveAlone"><dc:Bounds x="620" y="420" width="160" height="70"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_NotYours_di" bpmnElement="End_NotYours"><dc:Bounds x="840" y="437" width="36" height="36"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>

      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_1_di" bpmnElement="BF_1"><di:waypoint x="256" y="208"/><di:waypoint x="300" y="208"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_2_di" bpmnElement="BF_2"><di:waypoint x="450" y="208"/><di:waypoint x="490" y="208"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_3_di" bpmnElement="BF_3"><di:waypoint x="515" y="183"/><di:waypoint x="515" y="143"/><di:waypoint x="580" y="143"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_4_di" bpmnElement="BF_4"><di:waypoint x="515" y="233"/><di:waypoint x="515" y="278"/><di:waypoint x="620" y="278"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_5_di" bpmnElement="BF_5"><di:waypoint x="645" y="303"/><di:waypoint x="645" y="420"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_6_di" bpmnElement="BF_6"><di:waypoint x="780" y="455"/><di:waypoint x="840" y="455"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_7_di" bpmnElement="BF_7"><di:waypoint x="670" y="278"/><di:waypoint x="855" y="278"/><di:waypoint x="855" y="248"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_8_di" bpmnElement="BF_8"><di:waypoint x="730" y="143"/><di:waypoint x="855" y="143"/><di:waypoint x="855" y="168"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_9_di" bpmnElement="BF_9"><di:waypoint x="930" y="208"/><di:waypoint x="970" y="208"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_10_di" bpmnElement="BF_10"><di:waypoint x="1130" y="208"/><di:waypoint x="1170" y="208"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_11_di" bpmnElement="BF_11"><di:waypoint x="1195" y="183"/><di:waypoint x="1195" y="133"/><di:waypoint x="1270" y="133"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_12_di" bpmnElement="BF_12"><di:waypoint x="1220" y="208"/><di:waypoint x="1270" y="218"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_13_di" bpmnElement="BF_13"><di:waypoint x="1195" y="233"/><di:waypoint x="1195" y="313"/><di:waypoint x="1270" y="313"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_14_di" bpmnElement="BF_14"><di:waypoint x="1430" y="133"/><di:waypoint x="1518" y="133"/><di:waypoint x="1518" y="190"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_15_di" bpmnElement="BF_15"><di:waypoint x="1430" y="223"/><di:waypoint x="1500" y="210"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="BF_16_di" bpmnElement="BF_16"><di:waypoint x="1430" y="313"/><di:waypoint x="1518" y="313"/><di:waypoint x="1518" y="226"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
